  "summary": "The figure is an Arrhenius plot showing the temperature dependence of conductivity (\u03c3T) for LLBZT with varying doping levels (x = 0 to 0.30). The linear relationship indicates Arrhenius behavior. The undoped sample (x = 0, red squares) exhibits the highest conductivity across the measured temperature range (approx 300K to 370K), while the x = 0.30 sample (navy diamonds) shows the lowest. The slopes of the lines, indicative of activation energy, appear to slightly decrease (become less negative) with increasing x, suggesting a lower activation energy for higher doping levels despite the lower overall conductivity."
